:"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $F$ be an antiderivative of $f$ on an interval $I$. What is $\\displaystyle\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ on $I$?","options":["$F(x)+C$","$f(x)+C$","$F(x)$","$C\\,F(x)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3a82945b4b5107b548a17a5b","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_indefinite_integral_89f90687_005_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $F$ be an antiderivative of $f$ on an interval $I$. Why is $\\displaystyle\\int f(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ written as $F(x)+C$?","options":["Adding $C$ makes the antiderivative of $f$ unique","Every antiderivative of $f$ on $I$ equals $F+C$ for some constant $C$","The integrand $f$ is only known up to an additive constant","Some antiderivatives are $F+C$, but others differ from $F$ by a non-constant function"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c6dd1bd397f606a1df7fc9fd","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_indefinite_integral_89f90687_007_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which function belongs to the indefinite integral $\\displaystyle\\int 2x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$ on $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$x^2+x$","$2x^2$","$x^2+7$","$2x+7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a91a214970de373403b6ae3","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_indefinite_integral_89f90687_010_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"On $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ let $G(x)=\\ln|x|$ for $x<0$ and $G(x)=\\ln|x|+1$ for $x>0$. Which statement is correct?","options":["$G$ is not an antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{x}$, since antiderivatives differ by one constant","$G$ is not an antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{x}$, since it jumps at $0$","$G$ is an antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{x}$, though $G-\\ln|x|$ is not constant","$G'(x)=\\frac{1}{x}+1$ for $x>0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"54dc4c8471d9d55b5ec30baa","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_indefinite_integral_89f90687_020_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $\\displaystyle\\int 2\\sin x\\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, one student writes $\\sin^2x+C$ and another writes $-\\cos^2x+C$. Which is correct?","options":["Both, since $\\sin^2x-(-\\cos^2x)=1$ is a constant","Only $\\sin^2x+C$, since $(-\\cos^2x)'=-2\\sin x\\cos x$","Only $-\\cos^2x+C$, since $(\\sin^2x)'=2\\sin x$","Neither, since two different-looking answers cannot both be right"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9716c4e57d356fbd51b827b3","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_indefinite_integral_89f90687_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which function is an antiderivative of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ on the interval $(-\\infty,0)$?","options":["$\\ln(-x)$","$\\ln x$","$-\\ln(-x)$","$-\\frac{1}{x^2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"02f28e1b2f3e35b8da34e4bd","time_limit":30}]}}